      "problem": "Harvey orders $4$ pizzas for a party. If each pizza is cut so that a slice is $\\frac{1}{8}$ of a pizza, how many slices are there in total?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the total number of slices of pizza, we have to divide the number of pizzas by the size of each slice:\n\n$$\n4÷\\frac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nTo divide a whole number by a unit fraction, we multiply the whole number by the fraction's denominator:\n\n$$\n4÷\\frac{1}{8}=4\\times 8=32\n$$",
